    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate looking to capitalize on high-upside matchups, with **Yordan Alvarez** serving as our anchor at a 74.66 efficiency score. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a premier hitting environment and a favorable matchup against Perkins, whose profile allows for high-leverage production in the #2 spot. **Junior Caminero** remains a vital piece of our core at 66.70, maintaining a strong floor despite facing a quality arm in Aaron Nola. We are also leaning into the top-of-the-order potential of **Lars Nootbaar** (63.32) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (63.30); the former\u2019s platoon advantage against Walker Buehler and the latter\u2019s ability to exploit Lowder\u2019s 4.84 xERA suggest they are primary drivers for our run and RBI accumulation tonight.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Dillon Dingler**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 36.46 score. While his secondary indicators, such as a quick pop time and the potential for stolen bases against a slow-delivering pitcher, provided a slight lift, the negative impact of facing Yates and a poor platoon split ultimately pushed him below our 40.0 floor. We continue to monitor the status of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Christian Yelich**, all of whom are unavailable today due to schedule gaps or lineup rest, necessitating reliance on the depth provided by **Josh Smith**. While **Josh Smith** occupies the #7 spot, his 62.54 score is bolstered by his dynamic platoon utility and situational SB potential. \n\nManagers should remain cognizant of the risk inherent in **Carson Benge**\u2019s start (48.48), as his platoon disadvantage against a lefty arm creates a marginal efficiency profile. We are proceeding with the current lineup while holding reserves like **Colt Keith**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in the wings should late-breaking lineup changes occur. We have largely avoided elite-tier SPs today, giving **Trea Turner** and the rest of the squad a clearer path to exceeding base projections as we hunt for critical counting stats.",
